===persian===

آن آبشار سرخوش و مستم
که سال ها
بر ماسه های گرم تنت اشک ریختم
دیوانه وار
تا که بمیرم به دامنت
از دام برفهای سپیدم گریختم

وقتی شراب شیشه خورشید می چکید
برق تنم به تندی تیر نگاه بود

وقتی نگاه آینه مهر میشکست امواج سینه ام به سپیدی ماه بود افیون بادهای سحر پیکر مرا بی تاب مینمود در آغوش بسترم هر شاخه میگرفت به بازی تن مرا

هر برگ می گذشت به آسانی از سرم...

در تلخی زمانه چو شور تو داشتم چون شهد مینمود مرا انتظار تو می سوختم از گرمی آغوش این خیال دریای من تو بودی و من آبشار تو اکنون که در برابر من موج میزنی از خواب پر فریب تو بیدار میشوم تو مست و شاد از نگه آسمان و من در ساحل خموش تو در شن فرو روم

تابوت استخوانی سینه چو گور تنگ
در هم فشرده لاشه سرد غرور من

میگریم ای دریغ
چرا نیستم باز... من برف دره ها و
تو دریای دور من

۱۳۳۹

===machine===

That happy and drunk waterfall
that for years
I shed tears on the warm sands of your body
Like a madman
Until I die in your lap
I escaped from the trap of my white snow
When the wine dripped from the glass of the sun
The lightning of my body was as swift as a glance

When the look of the mirror of the seal broke, the waves of my chest were as white as the moon, the opium of the dawn winds made my body impatient in the embrace of my bed, every branch took my body to play with

Every leaf passed easily over my head...

In the bitterness of time, I was as thirsty as you, as if you were nectar, I was waiting for you, I was burning with the warmth of the embrace of this dream of my sea, you were and I am your waterfall, now that you are waving in front of me, I wake up from your deceptive sleep, you are drunk and happy from the hold of the sky and I sink into the sand on your silent shore

A coffin of bones, a chest like a narrow grave
The cold carcass of my pride, compressed together

We cry, oh my goodness
Why am I not here again... I am the snow of the valleys and
In the sea far away from me

1339

===lantern===

I am that giddy, drunken waterfall
who for years
wept onto the warm sands of your body,
wild with madness,
and to die at last in your lap
fled the snare of my own white snows.
When the wine dripped from the sun's glass
the lightning of my body was quick as a darted glance.

When the gaze in love's mirror shattered, the waves of my chest ran moon-white; the opium of the dawn winds left my body restless; in the embrace of my bed each branch took me up to play, and every leaf passed lightly over my head...

In the bitterness of the times I held your fever like a passion; waiting for you tasted to me like honey; I burned in the warmth of this dream's embrace. You were my sea and I your waterfall. Now that you surge before me I wake from your beguiling sleep — you, drunk and glad with the sky's regard, and I, on your silent shore, sinking into the sand.

The chest a coffin of bone, like a cramped grave,
the cold carcass of my pride pressed flat within it.

I weep — what a pity —
why am I no longer... I, the snow of the valleys, and you, my far-off sea?

1339

